12737 0 obj
<</Title(Project UDBHAVA represents a major advancement for Team Sammard, marking the team\220s transition to a fully student-researched and developed \(SRAD\) propulsion system while integrating a complex multi-subsystem architecture. The project successfully combines propulsion, aero-structures, avionics, recovery, payload, and ground systems into a cohesive launch vehicle designed for reliability and performance. Emphasis on modularity, subsystem validation, and system-level integration enabled the team to develop a robust design capable of meeting mission objectives. )/Dest[43 0 R/XYZ 72.083 630.22 0]/SE 1978 0 R/Parent 13480 0 R/Prev 12736 0 R/Next 12738 0 R>>
endobj

12738 0 obj
<</Title(Lessons Learned )/Dest[43 0 R/XYZ 72.2041 503.131 0]/SE 1981 0 R/Parent 13480 0 R/Prev 12737 0 R/Next 12739 0 R>>
endobj

12739 0 obj
<</Title(The development of UDBHAVA provided significant insights across both technical and team management domains. The transition to a fully SRAD propulsion system underscored the critical importance of repeatable manufacturing processes, disciplined grain casting procedures, and rigorous static fire validation in achieving predictable and consistent motor performance. A key lesson drawn from this subsystem was the necessity of an incremental development approach, where each component and process is individually validated before integration, ensuring that risks are identified and mitigated progressively rather than compounded at the system level.  )/Dest[43 0 R/XYZ 71.9658 491.078 0]/SE 1982 0 R/Parent 13480 0 R/Prev 12738 0 R/Next 12740 0 R>>
endobj

12740 0 obj
<</Title( )/Dest[43 0 R/XYZ 72 415.141 0]/SE 1983 0 R/Parent 13480 0 R/Prev 12739 0 R/Next 12741 0 R>>
endobj

12741 0 obj
<</Title(In aero-structures, precise manufacturing and alignment were found to be critical, particularly for load-bearing components and fin integration. Avionics development highlighted the need for robust state-machine logic, sensor redundancy, and noise-resistant algorithms to ensure reliable event detection and recovery system actuation. )/Dest[43 0 R/XYZ 72.0635 410.582 0]/SE 1984 0 R/Count 2/First 12742 0 R/Last 12743 0 R/Parent 13480 0 R/Prev 12740 0 R/Next 12744 0 R>>
endobj

