12782 0 obj
<</Title(The system is built around a Raspberry Pi, which runs the GCS software and interfaces with multiple peripherals through USB connections. These include a telemetry receiver PCB \(SHROTA\)  for acquiring flight data via LoRa communication and an ESP32 for transmitting GPS data to a mobile application for recovery purposes. The Cyberdeck also incorporates a display unit, keyboard, USB hub, and an uninterrupted power supply \(UPS\), ensuring continuous and reliable operation during outdoor missions. )/Dest[149 0 R/XYZ 72.0977 202.076 0]/SE 5152 0 R/Parent 12762 0 R/Prev 12781 0 R/Next 12783 0 R>>
endobj

12783 0 obj
<</Title(In addition to telemetry handling, the system integrates a separate video reception setup using another Raspberry Pi connected to an EasyCAP video receiver. This enables real-time video feed monitoring alongside telemetry data, enhancing overall mission awareness.  All components are securely housed within a custom 3D-printed structure, providing durability, organization, and ease of deployment in field environments. )/Dest[149 0 R/XYZ 71.9658 144.584 0]/SE 5153 0 R/Parent 12762 0 R/Prev 12782 0 R/Next 12784 0 R>>
endobj

12784 0 obj
<</Title(By combining telemetry reception, live video streaming, power management, and portability into a single unified system, the Cyberdeck acts as a robust and efficient control hub, supporting both monitoring and recovery operations throughout the mission lifecycle. )/Dest[150 0 R/XYZ 72.166 717.607 0]/SE 5154 0 R/Parent 12762 0 R/Prev 12783 0 R/Next 12785 0 R>>
endobj

